WEBVTT

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.000
The world is awash in pain.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:13.080
The Great War was the biggest war in human history,

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.380
and it left the world's nations with deep scars.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.000
Its conclusion brought about
a radical change in world affairs.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.540
I've got a special mission for you.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.250
As of tomorrow, you're splitting off
from the team for a solo op.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.040
It's what they call an Impossible Mission.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.250
The success rate on 'em is under ten percent,
and failure means death.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:42.830
You up for it?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.580
If those are your orders, Master, then consider it done.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.750
How about this, Idiot Pupil?

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.710
If you make it back alive, I've got a new title for you:

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.460
The Greatest Spy in the World.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.330
I'd say you will have earned it.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.540
It's got a nice ring to it, don't you think?

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.630
Magnificent.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.750
The politicians all realized how poor the
cost-performance of war was.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.170
Due to how advanced modern science was,
weapons were too effective at killing.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.630
With that, the era of nations pointing their guns at
each other out in the open came to an end...

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:34.000
Careful!

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:38.000
There's three guards.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.420
They're at range fifteen...

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:40.880
ten...

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:41.880
Got it!

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.330
Leave it to me, yo!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.330
Oh no, you don't.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:51.790
Yeep!

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.710
Someone was able to escape
Mr. Bernard's surveillance?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.500
That's gotta mean...

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:08.210
...we're dealing with a spy, and a good one.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.080
Let's do this!

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.710
Now, battles are fought between spies
over information

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.250
in shadow wars.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.000
<b>SPY CLASSROOM</b>

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:35.790
<b>MISSION: Flower Garden I</b>

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.380
It's been ten years since the Great War's end.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.960
Here in the Din Republic,

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.880
we've used that time to build spy academies

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.130
and put students through harsh training.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:44.040
But now, I finally get to graduate!

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.330
Yippee!

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.080
I'll remind you that it's only
a provisional graduation, Lily.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.250
There's a newly-formed spy team
that says they just have to have you.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.830
They did?

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:56.830
They did.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:01.250
As of today, the Cabinet Office is going
to be borrowing you for a bit.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.750
The notice says you'll learn the details on-site.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.170
It also said to wear those.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.830
Code name Flower Garden,

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.630
ready to put my life on the line, ma'am!

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.540
I gotta say, this outfit makes it feel more like
I'm transferring than graduating...

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.580
Still, though, I'm moving up in the world!

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.420
Hey mister, wait up!

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.460
<i>Eight years...</i>

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.750
<i>It's a wonder they kept me around so long
after I came so close to failing out so many times.</i>

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.920
Our next stop is Port City Arranq.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.540
We'll be arriving in Arranq soon.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.580
<i>I want to change.</i>

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.080
<i>I have to.</i>

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:08.540
All righty! Let's do this!

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:14.880
Excuse me! This is Garmouth Seminary, right?

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.210
I'm your awesome new transfer student!

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:20.750
Head on in.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.420
Now, the chapel should be right...

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.830
Here!

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:27.630
Here!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.040
Here?!

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.130
Th-this is bad!
I'm running late!

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.210
What a gorgeous manor...

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:09.380
I guess that's what the headquarters look like when the
Cabinet Office itself puts together a new spy team.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.630
Ah, I get it!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:16.790
This must be where all the talented
veteran spies are waiting for me!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.750
Oh no! We're supposed to be gathered by now!

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:23.580
Don't worry!

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.080
Code name Flower Garden is in the house!

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.420
A bunch of girls?

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.040
You're late.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.830
That isn't a good look for a spy.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.710
Looks like she's the last one.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.960
Yeah, and she's more of the same.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:47.920
Hey, you, with the silver hair.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.290
You got any field experience?

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.130
What were your academy grades like?

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.960
Wh-who, me?

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.380
I, uh, I'm here on a provisional graduation...

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.580
and to be honest, I was kind of a washout...

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.170
Figures.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.630
Well, join the club.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.880
Magnificent.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:15.830
Who's she?

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.080
Er, he?

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.830
And what's that red stuff on his clothes?

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.170
Thank you all for coming.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.710
This spy team is called Lamplight,

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.330
and I'm Klaus, the team's boss.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.630
Lamplight was put together to specialize
in Impossible Missions.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.420
Together, myself and the seven of you here
make up its full roster.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.080
One month from now,
we'll be taking on an Impossible Mission.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.790
Training starts tomorrow.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.880
For today, your job is to get to know your teammates.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.170
"Lamplight"?

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.630
What the hell's that guy thinkin'?

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:51.580
I mean, who goes and gathers up a bunch of
problem students to do an Impossible Mission with?

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:54.830
You heard me.
We're all washouts.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:57.920
Our academies were all too happy to get rid of us.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.210
What's this?

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:05.460
He left us something...

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.420
"Communal Living Rules"?

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.880
Wait, does that mean that...

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.750
Starting today!

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:13.790
We all!

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:14.880
Get!

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.380
To live here?!

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:20.250
Let's start by having dinner together, then!

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:30.540
So, all seven of us are from different academies?

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:32.080
<b>Pandemonium</b>

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.080
That's a weird coincidence.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.670
Actually, I suspect that isn't a coincidence at all...

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:35.670
<b>Daughter Dearest</b>

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:38.880
Yeah! I think so too, yo.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.880
<b>Forgetter</b>

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.380
The one thing we have in common is, we're all washouts.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:42.380
<b>Meadow</b>

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:45.750
For the record, I was half-assing it on purpose.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.630
<b>Glint</b>

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.580
There's something strange about the manor, too.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:50.170
<b>Dreamspeaker</b>

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:50.170
There are traces of people having lived here.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.250
Isn't it swanky, though?

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:54.290
<b>Flower Garden</b>

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:54.290
We each get a room all to ourselves!

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.540
No, no, there's something fishy about all this!

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.500
I mean, Impossible Missions...

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:02.790
...are difficult tasks with mortality rates of
over ninety percent, even for first-rate spies.

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:06.830
Why do one with an entire group of
underperforming washouts?

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.750
C'mon, it'll be fine!

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.460
That Klaus guy was practically radiating competence.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:17.250
I'm sure he's going to do a great job training us all up.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.790
I don't know about that...

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.380
Just think about it.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:23.080
We all tried hard back at our academies, didn't we?

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:25.790
I suppose?

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:26.790
Aight!

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.750
Starting tomorrow, let's kill it out there!

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.080
Yeah!

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.000
I can see that you've all gotten to know each other.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:02.920
Today, we start our training.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.540
Before we get into all that,
I've got some questions.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.960
What is this mission we're going on?

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:11.080
And why exactly did you pick us?

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:12.750
It's as you can see.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.960
I can't give you any specifics right now.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:19.750
One month from now, we'll be infiltrating
the hostile Galgad Empire

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.540
and completing an Impossible Mission.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.540
At the moment, that's all I can tell you.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.290
That's not much of an explanation.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.170
There's no need to be so worried.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.790
Here, let me show you why.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.630
Can any of you open these?

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:44.080
Wait, this mechanism is way too tricky.

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:46.250
It'd take me at least fifteen minutes to-

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:01.670
Once you've taken my lessons,
you'll be able to do the same in no time.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.250
Wow...

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.880
So, that's what a first-rate spy looks like in action!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.920
Over the next month,
I'll be training you here in Heat Haze Palace

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:14.000
until you're strong enough to
complete Impossible Missions.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.130
Does anyone still have reservations?

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:19.460
No, sir!
Oh, I'm so glad I came here!

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:20.960
Good.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:23.040
Now, as far as the lockpicking lesson goes...

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.830
...just use your picking tool correctly.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:28.380
That concludes the lesson.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.330
Uh, run that by me again?

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.670
And a little more clearly, perhaps?

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:40.080
That concludes the lesson.

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:44.330
As you can see, the locks will open
if you use your picking tool correctly.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.630
I trust you see that now.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.790
You should make like a honeybee tickling a stamen,

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.290
to be more specific.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.500
Don't tell me...

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.710
Um, Teach, we were hoping for
more of an explanation.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.080
But I just gave you one.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:02.710
Were you really unable to follow it?

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:05.670
I see.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:10.750
Well, I was thinking about having the next set of lectures
be the "talk beautifully" lesson on negotiation,

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.170
the "just take them down" lesson on combat,

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:16.250
and the "it'll all work out" lesson on disguises.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.920
Do you think you'll be able to follow any of them?

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:18.920
Nope.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.380
And the rest of you?

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:24.330
I see.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:25.670
Magnificent.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:29.420
I'm only just learning this, but apparently,
I'm quite bad at teaching.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.500
The rest of the day will be self-study.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.830
Hold on one dang second!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.750
Is that guy off his rocker?

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.500
How the hell are we supposed to complete
this Impossible Mission?!

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.290
This is bad...

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:49.500
Pretty sure we're gonna get slaughtered, yo!

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:50.710
I agree.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.040
I don't like it, but that's where we stand.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.880
Settle down, everyone.

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:56.630
I'm sure Teach has some sort of plan.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:59.630
I-I think I figured it out.

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:04.040
We have a group of washouts and
a teacher who can't teach.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:05.710
I think...

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:07.920
I think he's using us as sacrificial pawns!

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:13.290
That teacher of ours has no intention of
getting the seven of us out alive!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.380
How did it come to this?

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:28.920
<i>I mean, I became a spy because
I wanted to change the world.</i>

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:30.960
<i>And plus...</i>

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.330
<i>If we're just going to die,</i>

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:36.580
<i>then what did we even bother getting driven out
of our academies and coming here for?</i>

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:38.920
I refuse to die here.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.960
We might be washouts, but we still have dreams,

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.630
and we still have our pride.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:48.960
I'm code name Flower Garden...

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.210
and it's time to bloom out of control.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:56.920
<b>MISSION: Flower Garden I</b>

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.080
Hello?

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:07.500
What do you want?

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.710
Uh...

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:10.920
As for me, it's as you can see.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:12.540
What is?

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:15.630
I'm trying to come up with new teaching methods.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:19.710
It definitely just looks like you're painting.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:24.920
<i>He titled it "Family"?</i>

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.460
Oh hey, books about education?

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:30.670
I guess you're actually taking this pretty seriously.

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:32.630
Got any ideas yet?

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:34.040
Not a one.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.290
It's quite the quandary.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:40.420
In that case, Teach, how about we go sightseeing?

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:41.630
I don't follow.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.080
You know, as a breather.

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:46.330
A nice change of pace can help the creative juices flow.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:48.210
I can't say the idea speaks to me, but...

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:49.960
Did you have anywhere in mind?

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:52.540
Yeah! I made a list of all the local attractions!

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.380
You know what?

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:57.790
You have a point.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.080
Let's take a little break tomorrow.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:01.630
Great!

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:09.000
Whoa, so this is the famous Maple Lane!

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.250
There are so many people here!

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:11.460
What a pain in the butt!

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:16.170
Sorry, I didn't mean to say that last bit out loud...

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:19.080
I expected the others to be here, too.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.540
Is it just you?

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.960
Yeah, they all turned me down.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.290
In that case, let's get them
some souvenirs before we go.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.460
Good idea! What should we get?

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:29.000
That's an excellent question...

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:30.580
What about some canned goods?

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:34.170
Thanks to recent advances in
vacuum-sealing technology,

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:36.580
we've been getting some excellent imports
these past few years.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:39.460
Sardines canned in oil pair fantastically with pasta.

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:40.830
Oh?

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:42.290
After you boil your pasta,

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:46.250
you can take a frying pan and fry up some
chopped vegetables with your sardines.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:48.710
Once you've boiled off most of the juices,

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:51.210
all you have to do is pour it over your pasta
and add spices to taste.

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:53.210
Ooh, that sounds tasty.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:55.710
Hey, wait! You explained that recipe just fine!

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.130
Thief!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.540
Someone, stop him!

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.380
Huh?!

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:07.580
Damn it!

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:09.830
Here.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:11.380
He dropped this.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.380
Oh, you're too kind!

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.670
Tell me, how'd you do that just now?

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.170
I just did.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:26.040
How did you put on your shirt this morning?

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:28.790
I mean, I put my arm in the sleeve-

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.000
Which arm did you start with?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:31.630
Did you rotate your waist?

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:33.130
Did you bend your back?

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:34.750
I, uh...

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.250
How did you do up your buttons?
What about your collar?

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:39.710
H-how am I supposed to answer that?

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.000
I just did.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.290
And that's precisely how I feel.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:48.750
Wait, you're saying that you did that thing just now
and the lockpicking yesterday

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.460
without having to consciously think about it?

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:54.330
Exactly, I can say that I used the picking tool correctly,

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:59.460
but there's no way for me to come up with specific,
systemic explanations that would make sense to others,

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:01.920
because I performed the actions on instinct.

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:04.380
So in other words,

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.630
the problem is that your intuition is just too darn good?

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:13.210
But that means there really is
no way you'll be able to teach us...

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.540
Remember, Teach, we're here to take a load off!

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.670
To forget all about our pesky problems!

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.080
You seem quite adept at that.

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:31.080
Ooh, look at that!

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.130
The sunset is so pretty.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.580
Let's go there next!

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:42.380
Looks like it's super crowded here, too!

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:46.250
This is Emai Lake, the most popular
tourist attraction in the region.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:49.000
If you take a boat to the middle of the lake,

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:52.000
you can enjoy Mother Nature in all her splendor.

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:53.670
How sophisticated.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:57.880
With how crowded it is, though,
I suspect all the rental boats will be taken.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.630
No, look!

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:04.500
Today's our lucky day!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.250
There's one boat left!

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:07.960
Hold on, Lily.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.580
It's the man's job to get in first,
make sure it's safe...

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:17.130
and offer the lady his hand.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:30.960
Wow, it's so pretty.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:34.080
Never forget this sight, Lily.

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:38.250
Never forget the natural views so picturesque
that you want to embrace them.

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:41.040
Never forget the smiles you saw at the market.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:45.420
Never forget the people cherishing their loved ones
under the setting sun's light.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:46.830
Teach?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:51.170
Someone once planted a bomb in
that very same Maple Lane.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:55.750
They were an Imperial agent trying to
assassinate one of our politicians.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:59.630
And the people who promptly got ahold of
that intel and put a stop to the plot...

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:02.380
...were our fellow spies from the Republic?

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.880
This world of ours is awash in pain.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.670
The war's scars still linger,

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:10.750
but our people are slowly starting
to find their smiles again.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:14.500
The only people who can protect them are spies like us.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.380
Never forget that.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:19.460
So, what, I should just become a sacrificial pawn?

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:25.460
That's why you gathered up a
bunch of washouts, right?

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:29.920
But if I die now,
then my whole life will have been for nothing.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:34.540
The only thing that got me through those
harsh years at the academy

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:36.750
was the idea that someday, I'd be able to bloom.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:38.540
Lily?

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:41.210
I get how important this mission must be,

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:43.170
but I'm sorry.

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:46.250
I can't accompany you, Teach.

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:48.000
I really, truly mean it.

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:50.210
I'm code name Flower Garden,

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:52.630
and it's time to bloom out of control.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:56.420
Poison gas?

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:00.790
Don't you worry.

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:03.080
It's just a paralytic.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.250
It won't kill you.

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:05.710
I don't get it...

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:07.210
You got hit too!

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:10.130
This poison doesn't work on me.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.210
I've got an abnormal physiology.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:21.080
That was how I became my village's
sole survivor during the Great War.

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:22.750
This is inhuman.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:26.750
Those Imperial bastards used this place as
a testing ground for their new weapon!

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:29.210
Hey, there's someone still alive!

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:41.630
Back then, a spy saved my life.

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:47.710
The only reason the army sent a team there was
because spies told them what had happened.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.630
That's why I've been trying so hard.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.960
I want to become a spy and save my country.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.580
I want to change the world, even just a little.

00:19:57.580 --> 00:20:00.580
But when we spent the day together,
I became sure of something.

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:02.540
You can't teach.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:07.130
If we stay on Lamplight, we're just going to die.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:09.630
I'm a poison specialist.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:13.500
Your defeat was sealed
the moment you got on this boat.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:15.540
What are you hoping to achieve?

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:17.210
I want Lamplight disbanded.

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:20.460
And I want you to get us all jobs on other spy teams.

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:22.630
I'm sure that's within your power.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.750
Someone's certainly feeling greedy.

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:28.000
If you won't cooperate,
I'll stab you with this poison needle.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.790
It'll put you out like a light.

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:31.960
So, your goal is to survive?

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.170
That's right, I'm sorry about this,

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.330
but it was the only way.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.580
Come on, Teach!

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:42.380
Recognize that you've lost and agree to do what I-

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.290
I recognize your efforts, certainly.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:45.960
But I have to ask...

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:49.040
how much longer should I keep
playing along with this game?

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:55.170
Shackles?

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.420
When did you set those up?

00:20:58.170 --> 00:20:59.500
We're sinking?!

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:01.080
Last night.

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:03.580
In spite of its incredible popularity,

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:08.960
Emai Lake was conspicuously absent from
that sightseeing list you gave me.

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:11.380
It stank to high heaven.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:15.670
And if you were going to pull something
in a place as busy as this lake,

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:18.960
the logical place to do it would be on a boat
where you could make sure nobody else was around.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.500
It was an obvious enough conclusion.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:22.420
I played things too safe.

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:26.500
I left the lake off my list so you couldn't
predict where I would attack you,

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.540
but it looks like that backfired.

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:29.830
But still!

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:31.630
How could you have known we would take this boat?!

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:36.790
"Out Of Order"?!

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:41.420
It's hard to see from your seat,
but it's plain as day to the rower.

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:44.040
This boat was always going to be the last one left.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:45.710
You set all this up last night?

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:48.710
Wait, you did that to divert my attention?!

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:51.580
Don't bother.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:54.210
You already showed me your limits.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:58.380
You aren't qualified to be my enemy, Lily.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.000
On top of all that,

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.710
I realized you were plotting to attack me
the moment you came to my room last night.

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:08.080
But how?

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:09.750
I just did.

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:13.040
I'm such an idiot for expecting anything out of you!

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:15.250
Hurry up and give me the antidote.

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:16.790
The boat's going to sink soon.

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:18.290
Fine.

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:19.920
You win.

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:24.290
What is it?

00:22:24.750 --> 00:22:25.920
It, uh...

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:28.830
It looks like I might have accidently left it in my room.

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:32.170
You got a key for these shackles, Teach?

00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:34.170
Not on me.

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:37.710
If you found it while I was immobilized,
I would lose my leverage.

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:41.710
I figured I could unlock you myself
once I got the antidote.

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:43.330
Uh, that's...

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:45.500
N-nothing to worry about!

00:22:45.500 --> 00:22:48.170
In ten minutes, the poison will have worked
its way out of your system all on its-

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:51.040
Incidentally, we have five minutes until the boat sinks.

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:55.420
Row like your life depends on it.

00:22:55.420 --> 00:22:56.790
After all, it does.

00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:06.750
I lost completely...

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:11.290
I guess it's once a washout, always a washout.

00:23:11.920 --> 00:23:13.420
Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:15.290
That was some excellent poison.

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:18.750
Yeah, but you probably let yourself
get hit on purpose, didn't you?

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:21.080
I did. I wanted to test your skills.

00:23:23.210 --> 00:23:26.040
This situation couldn't get worse.

00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:31.330
We're terrible students, you suck at teaching,

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:33.830
and Impossible Missions are as deadly as they come.

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:37.380
I guess I just have to give up.

00:23:37.710 --> 00:23:41.880
And all I wanted was to bloom into
a spy I could be proud of.

00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:48.210
Not at all.

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:51.830
You have what it takes.

00:23:52.460 --> 00:23:54.880
Our battle may have been little more than a game,

00:23:54.880 --> 00:23:58.130
but the fact you saw the impending crisis
and took steps to prevent it faster than anyone else

00:23:58.130 --> 00:23:59.630
was unreservedly...

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:01.920
magnificent.

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:04.790
Fl-flattery will get you nowhere, you know!

00:24:04.790 --> 00:24:08.210
Lily, I want you to become Lamplight's leader.

00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:12.330
I'll still be the team's boss,

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:15.130
but we need someone for
the rest of you to rally around.

00:24:15.130 --> 00:24:17.630
Let's work together to make this mission a success.

00:24:18.630 --> 00:24:20.170
Ooh, leader...

00:24:20.170 --> 00:24:22.000
That sounds so cool...

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:25.330
But what's this about completing the mission?

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:28.500
You still can't teach you way out of a-

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:31.080
Actually, I solved that problem.

00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:37.290
I just came up with a new teaching method,
and it's all thanks to you, Flower Garden Lily.

00:24:41.290 --> 00:24:46.080
Now, I've gathered you all here again,
and it's as you can see.

00:24:47.750 --> 00:24:49.000
What is?

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:50.290
I'm apologizing.

00:24:50.290 --> 00:24:52.210
Not sure how we're supposed to see that...

00:24:53.170 --> 00:24:57.040
My poor explanations caused a misunderstanding,
and I'd like to start by clearing it up.

00:24:57.420 --> 00:24:59.830
None of you are sacrificial pawns.

00:25:01.210 --> 00:25:06.630
Everyone's going to live, and we're going to
complete that Impossible Mission.

00:25:06.960 --> 00:25:10.540
That's what I hand-selected this group
of magnificent members for.

00:25:10.920 --> 00:25:12.750
I'm not going to let a single one of you die.

00:25:12.750 --> 00:25:16.080
B-but I heard that Impossible Missions

00:25:16.080 --> 00:25:19.580
have a ninety percent mortality rate,
even for first-rate spies.

00:25:19.790 --> 00:25:21.960
There's no way we survive-

00:25:21.960 --> 00:25:23.750
That's what you have me for.

00:25:24.880 --> 00:25:27.750
I'm no paltry first-rate spy.

00:25:28.130 --> 00:25:31.130
I'm the Greatest Spy in the World.

00:25:32.250 --> 00:25:34.540
If we work together,

00:25:34.540 --> 00:25:36.920
this Impossible Mission is going to be child's play.

00:25:37.210 --> 00:25:38.880
"The Greatest Spy in the World"?

00:25:38.880 --> 00:25:40.080
What does that even mean?

00:25:40.080 --> 00:25:41.960
It sounds so childish.

00:25:42.130 --> 00:25:43.380
Don't worry.

00:25:43.380 --> 00:25:49.080
Teach is going to lead Lamplight to greatness.

00:25:49.290 --> 00:25:52.170
As your team leader, I guarantee it.

00:25:54.460 --> 00:25:58.960
I've already figured out a curriculum
that will improve your skills.

00:26:00.830 --> 00:26:02.920
Defeat me.

00:26:03.790 --> 00:26:07.790
And that marked our first step as spies

00:26:08.170 --> 00:26:10.210
into a classroom of deception.
